<!-- Part 14 e2e scenario: the positive counterpart to
     test_vt_datatype_sibling_override.NodeSet2. Declares a genuine two-level
     custom DataType subtype chain, GenericCodeType (subtype of the real
     opcua:Enumeration) and SpecificCodeType (subtype of GenericCodeType, not
     a sibling of anything). BaseType declares Mandatory "Code" :
     PropertyType/GenericCodeType. SubType, a subtype of BaseType, narrows
     "Code" to PropertyType/SpecificCodeType, exactly the legal move OPC
     UA's DataType-override rule allows (narrowing to a genuine subtype).

     VT(SubType, "Code") ends up:
       - rdfs:subClassOf [ allValuesFrom SpecificCodeType ]
       - rdfs:subClassOf VT(BaseType, "Code"), itself subClassOf
         [ allValuesFrom GenericCodeType ]
     Since SpecificCodeType rdfs:subClassOf GenericCodeType (a real subtype,
     not a disjoint sibling), this is unconditionally consistent: no
     AllDisjointClasses set ever contains both types together (each has
     exactly one direct subtype of its own in this file, so
     _add_datatype_disjointness has nothing to assert disjoint at either
     level). Audits that a correct, spec-legal narrowing produces no
     false-positive contradiction, the DataType-axis mirror of
     test_vt_override.NodeSet2's plain type-override case. -->
